{
  "version": 1,
  "date": "2026-08-04",
  "brief": "A3 - parity arm + gold: olmOCR toolkit (allenai/olmOCR-2-7B-1025)",
  "harness": "tests/score_gold_transcripts.py (imports normalize/score/summarize/render_markdown from tests/ocr_external_parity.py)",
  "gold": "tests/regression/gold/olmocr/{synth,cc0}",
  "kernels": [
    "tools/kaggle/olmocr-parity (gold + contract capture)",
    "tools/kaggle/olmocr-vllm-probe (serving-layer probe)"
  ],
  "repro": [
    "# local: the toolkit itself, for the CPU-side contract capture",
    "~/miniconda3/bin/python -m venv ~/venvs/olmocr && ~/venvs/olmocr/bin/pip install olmocr",
    "# wrap each labelled fixture into a single-page PDF (lossless embed)",
    "img2pdf --output <stem>.pdf <fixture image>   # img2pdf 0.6.3",
    "# reference run (Kaggle GPU, chr1s4)",
    "KAGGLE_API_TOKEN=<chr1s4> python -c \"from kaggle import KaggleApi; a=KaggleApi(); a.authenticate(); print(a.kernels_push('tools/kaggle/olmocr-parity'))\"",
    "# scoring, offline, from the retrieved transcripts",
    "python tests/score_gold_transcripts.py --images ~/crispembed-ocr-synth --gold tests/regression/gold/olmocr/synth --engine olmocr-toolkit --strip-markup --output /tmp/olmocr_synth.json",
    "python tests/score_gold_transcripts.py --images tests/regression/images/cc0 --gold tests/regression/gold/olmocr/cc0 --engine olmocr-toolkit --strip-markup --output /tmp/olmocr_cc0.json"
  ],
  "notes": [
    "NO TIMING COLUMN HERE IS A LATENCY MEASUREMENT. `generation_s` is wall time for one transformers generate() call on a Kaggle 2x T4 pair with the weights split across both cards by accelerate - a model-parallel pipeline, not a serving configuration. It is recorded so a page that took 69 s is visible, and for no other purpose. It must never be quoted next to a Mac number or next to the toolkit's own vLLM throughput.",
    "The serving layer is a deviation from the toolkit: olmocr[gpu] pins vllm==0.11.2 and generation here ran through transformers 4.57.3 (the version that same extra pins). The *request* is not a deviation - it is built by importing olmocr.pipeline.build_page_query, so prompt, message order, render and sampling params are the toolkit's own code.",
    "The checkpoint is a deviation: the toolkit defaults to allenai/olmOCR-2-7B-1025-FP8 whose quantised kernels need sm_89+; the unquantised sibling ran instead.",
    "fp16, not the checkpoint's bf16: the cards are compute capability 7.5, where torch emulates bf16. Same open follow-up as the Qwen2.5-VL arm.",
    "The primary CER keeps the markdown/HTML the prompt asks for, because that is what the arm returns to a caller. cer_markup_stripped is a diagnostic second view: on commons_example_receipt.png the model emitted the receipt table as <table> markup exactly as instructed, which plain-text CER charges at 0.70 while the words are right (0.00983 stripped). Note the stripping is not free: on receipt_historical.png it removes real characters and the stripped CER is slightly worse (0.05469 -> 0.06120), so quote both.",
    "Every one of the 25 pages passed the toolkit's validity rules on attempt 0 in both passes, so no page in this gold was produced at temperature > 0 and none is a pdftotext fallback.",
    "The gold ships from the transformers pass rather than the vLLM one because vLLM returns a truncated simple_form.png (CER 0.37247 vs 0.04858) while claiming finish_reason 'stop'. Both sets are in the gold directory; vllm-serving/ is the toolkit's actual stack and is the reason no gate may be a byte diff."
  ],
